comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T08:13:08.155Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: searched all statuses for GH-1135, GH-1040, GH-1004, GH-976, item_hash_version, writer-version repair loops, and changed=false byte rewrites; fully read closed pm-0wfdim, pm-igdvfq, and pm-2htk4p. Those owners implemented epoch-aware verification and repair, while #1135 is a fresh post-fix three-repository reproduction that names same-version-marker hash divergence and a false repair receipt. This open unclaimed recurrence is canonical for GitHub #1135."
  "2026-08-28T08:13:51.701Z","harness:codex","GitHub linkage evidence: #1135 comment https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1135#issuecomment-5450113598 points to this canonical PM item and its merge-stable main-branch .toon path."
  "2026-08-28T23:24:18.291Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence: focused history and recovery suites passed; live pm validate checked 2,596 items with zero history drift and zero version skew in the current workspace; full repository coverage passed 8,099 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-29T02:22:13.930Z","harness:codex","Review-round evidence: unsupported cache epochs now invalidate even when older rows omit version_skew, and compatible-version chain corruption remains independently visible instead of being masked by writer skew. Focused regressions passed; current-head coverage passed 586 files and 8,105 tests at exactly 60,136/60,136 statements, 45,331/45,331 branches, 12,503/12,503 functions, and 57,907/57,907 lines."
  "2026-08-29T04:41:15.281Z","harness:codex","Review-round finding: Greptile exact head 89031f identified that mixed-version streams still suppress an independently checkable final supported after_hash mismatch. Reopened to preserve both version-skew and item-drift evidence."
  "2026-08-29T05:25:24.096Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: the scanner continues past an unsupported earlier epoch for the independent final supported after_hash comparison. Focused linked tests passed 39 assertions (11 connected plus 28 history); the exact repository coverage run passed 8,111 tests at 60,140/60,140 statements, 45,357/45,357 branches, 12,505/12,505 functions, and 57,911/57,911 lines."
  "2026-08-29T06:08:46.316Z","harness:codex","Final CodeRabbit review finding: drift cache loading accepts non-boolean chain_ok values, allowing truthy malformed metadata to bypass chain mismatch detection. Reopened for strict cache schema validation and a negative control."
  "2026-08-29T06:28:53.971Z","harness:codex","Final review evidence: drift cache decoding now rejects non-boolean chain_ok values. The focused four-file review suite passed 103/103, full coverage passed 8,112 tests at 100/100/100/100, repository quality:static passed, and linked acceptance passed."
  "2026-08-29T07:13:38.431Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit exact-head finding: new history version-skew health and validate codes lack registry guidance, leaving agents without the safe runtime-upgrade command. Reopened for executable remediation parity."
  "2026-08-29T07:43:02.400Z","harness:codex","Review closure evidence: registered executable npm upgrade remediation for both health history_drift_version_skew and validate_history_drift_version_skews, regenerated the error catalog, refusal census, contract fixture, and SDK surface, and proved the registry regression. Full repository result: 586 files and 8,113 tests passed at exact 100/100/100/100 coverage (60,145 statements, 45,362 branches, 12,508 functions, 57,915 lines)."
learnings[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T23:24:36.998Z","harness:codex","Persisted hash algorithms are format capabilities, not implementation details. Any hash-input change must advance the writer epoch so readers can classify skew separately from corruption."
  "2026-08-29T05:25:24.557Z","harness:codex","History capability skew and current-item divergence are independent evidence: an unsupported earlier event must not erase a safely comparable final supported after_hash."
  "2026-08-29T06:28:53.527Z","harness:codex","Persisted caches are untrusted inputs: validate every required scalar type before reusing a cached integrity verdict, even when version and fingerprint fields match."
  "2026-08-29T07:43:02.818Z","harness:codex","A newer history hash capability is a runtime compatibility boundary, not repairable corruption; every health and validation projection must route to upgrade guidance rather than history-repair."
